{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>My bow I have set in the cloud.</b> I have arranged it so that it comes to be in nature." "<b>And it shall be a sign of the covenant.</b> When the bow is doubled — for indeed the scholars of inquiry despaired of giving a reason for the order of the colors of the second bow, which is the reverse of the order of colors of the familiar first bow — and it shall be a sign for the righteous of the generation whose generation is liable, as they said (Ketuvot 77b): 'Was the bow seen in your days?' — so that they may pray and rebuke and teach knowledge to the people."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:29:43.654430308Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}